{{- /* Which registry entries THIS machine's running macOS is too old to install, as a
       JSON array of {"name", "type", "min_macos"} objects — every field the two
       consumers (the Brewfile's selection pass, dotfiles-doctor) need to match an
       entry and explain why it's missing. Scoped to all of .pkg.packages regardless
       of bundles, since intersecting with an enabled/tracked set is each consumer's
       own job and doing it here would make this partial mean something different to
       each caller.

       Rendered at RENDER time, not install time — see run_onchange_install-
       packages.sh.tmpl's own header. Its Brewfile hash line has to move when this
       partial's answer changes, or an OS upgrade never re-triggers the install that
       was blocked. Reading the OS version at install time instead would leave that
       hash exactly where it was on the old OS forever.

       FAIL OPEN. semverCompare hard-errors on anything that isn't a clean semantic
       version ("invalid semantic version"), and a template error here doesn't just
       skip a filter — it kills every `chezmoi apply` on the machine, including the
       ones that install nothing gated by this at all. So every path that can't
       produce a trustworthy version string bails to an empty array before
       semverCompare is ever called, and holding nothing back is exactly today's
       behavior for a machine with no such guard at all. */ -}}
{{- $held := list -}}
{{- $ver := "" -}}
{{- if lookPath "sw_vers" -}}
{{-   $raw := output "sw_vers" "-productVersion" | trim -}}
{{-   if regexMatch "^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)*$" $raw -}}
{{-     $ver = $raw -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if $ver -}}
{{-   range $p := .pkg.packages -}}
{{-     if and (hasKey $p "min_macos") (ne $p.min_macos "") -}}
{{-       if not (semverCompare (printf ">=%s" $p.min_macos) $ver) -}}
{{-         $held = append $held (dict "name" $p.name "type" $p.type "min_macos" $p.min_macos) -}}
{{-       end -}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $held | toJson -}}
